🚀 Quick start
You can run this lab on any recent Linux or macOS machine with Python 3.11+ installed. A few convenient make targets orchestrate the entire workflow. First clone the repository, then run the following commands:

bash
Copy
Edit
# Install dependencies and prepare pre‑commit hooks
make setup

# (optional) generate fresh synthetic logs for a clean experiment
make demo-data

# Ingest the raw logs into an intermediate parquet file
make ingest

# Engineer session level features from the ingested logs
make featurize

# Run TPOT’s genetic search to build the best classifier (may take ~20 mins)
make automl

# Evaluate the exported pipeline and produce plots
make evaluate

# Start the FastAPI inference server on http://localhost:8000
make serve

# Query the API with a sample feature vector
curl -X POST localhost:8000/predict -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
     -d '{"req_per_min": 18, "unique_endpoints": 7, "cmd_entropy": 3.4, "default_creds_attempts": 5}'
