💡 60‑second overview
The honeypot component spins up a tiny HTTP server and a dummy SSH listener on arbitrary high ports. It logs every request with timestamps, IP addresses, requested endpoints, user‑agent strings and crude SSH credential attempts. A parser normalises these logs into a structured table. Feature engineering scripts aggregate requests into sessions and compute high‑level statistics: request rates, endpoint diversity, command entropy, default credential attempts, and temporal features. A simple heuristic labelling function marks obviously malicious sessions (e.g. those hammering default credentials or scanning many endpoints) to bootstrap supervised learning.

Using TPOT, a genetic algorithm based AutoML tool, the pipeline then searches over a space of scikit‑learn model architectures to maximise an F1 score on the weakly labelled data. The resulting model is exported as both Python code and a pickled pipeline. Finally, a small FastAPI app loads the model and exposes a /predict endpoint that accepts JSON feature vectors and returns class predictions with confidence scores and the top contributing features when available.

⚠ Ethics & safety
This repository intentionally implements a low‑interaction honeypot. It does not emulate full services, nor does it attempt to trick or entrap attackers. Its purpose is to generate benign synthetic attack traffic for research and educational purposes. Do not deploy this code on production networks or to internet‑facing infrastructure without proper isolation. Running a honeypot can have legal and ethical implications depending on your jurisdiction. Always separate honeypot traffic from sensitive systems and obtain appropriate approvals before collecting real attack data.

🔧 Make targets
Key tasks are defined in the Makefile for convenience:

Target	Purpose
setup	Install dependencies via uv (or pip fallback) and set up pre‑commit
demo-data	Generate fresh synthetic log files in data/raw
ingest	Parse logs from data/raw into data/interim parquet
featurize	Engineer features from sessions into data/processed
automl	Train a TPOT pipeline and export the best model
evaluate	Compute metrics and save ROC/PR curves
serve	Launch the FastAPI server on localhost:8000
test	Run the unit tests with pytest
lint	Run Ruff and Black style checks
format	Format code using Black
clean	Remove generated data and models

