Makefile: convenience targets for setup, data generation, ingestion, feature engineering, AutoML training, evaluation, serving, linting, testing, and Docker: Makefile

CI workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml): GitHub Actions configuration for installing dependencies, running linters, tests, generating synthetic data, training a quick TPOT model, evaluating it, uploading artifacts, and building the Docker image: ci.yml

Starter scripts:

Honeypot runner (src/honeypot/run_honeypot.py): spawns minimal HTTP and SSH listeners, logging to data/raw: run_honeypot.py

Log parser (src/honeypot/log_parser.py): parses raw logs into a normalized DataFrame and writes parquet/CSV; also generates synthetic demo logs: log_parser.py

Feature engineering (src/honeypot/feature_engineering.py): aggregates events per IP, computes statistics (request rate, endpoint diversity, entropy, default-credential attempts, user-agent rarity, temporal features), and applies weak labels: feature_engineering.py

Labeling heuristics (src/honeypot/labeling.py): simple rules for benign/malicious classification with YAML overrides: labeling.py

TPOT training script (src/automl/train_tpot.py): runs TPOT AutoML search with configurable hyperparameters, exports the best pipeline as Python code and a pickled model, saves metrics and plots: train_tpot.py

Evaluation script (src/automl/eval.py): evaluates a trained model on a feature dataset, computing metrics and generating ROC/PR curves: eval.py

FastAPI service (src/api/serve.py): loads the trained model and exposes /health, /version, and /predict endpoints for inference: serve.py
